READ THIS FIRST: THE CODE IS DUAL-LICENSED

  The software in this repository (src/, tests/, and the build configuration)
  is available under EITHER of:

      MIT License                                    (full text below)
      Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International  (see LICENSE-DOCS)

  You may choose either one. SPDX: MIT OR CC-BY-4.0

  Documentation, notebooks and figures are licensed under CC BY 4.0 alone.
  See LICENSE-DOCS.

WHY DUAL, AND NOT JUST ONE

  Two requirements pull in opposite directions, and both are legitimate.

  The Rare Disease, Real Kid: MVA Hackathon 2026 rules place submissions,
  including code and reports, under a CC BY licence, with the author's name
  shared as part of the open-access attribution. A repository whose code was
  MIT-only would not satisfy that, so an earlier version of this file was
  non-compliant.

  Creative Commons, for its part, explicitly recommends against applying its
  licences to software, because they do not address source-code distribution
  or patent rights:
  https://creativecommons.org/faq/#can-i-apply-a-creative-commons-license-to-software

  Offering both resolves it without weakening either. Everything in this
  repository is available under CC BY 4.0, which is what the hackathon
  requires; and anyone who wants to reuse the code in software gets MIT, which
  is what a software licence is actually built for. The recipient picks.

